.TH CLAUDE-AGENTS-TRAY 1 2026-10-31 "claude-agents-indicator 0.3.0"
.SH NAME
claude-agents-tray \- tray icon for the Claude Code sessions waiting on you
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-agents-tray
.RB [ \-\-jump ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-agents-tray
puts a StatusNotifierItem in the system tray. Its menu lists the sessions from
.BR "claude agents" ,
grouped as Needs You, Your Turn and Working, with the 5-hour and weekly usage
when available. The icon switches to its attention state, and the label shows
the count, while a session needs you.
.PP
Clicking a session selects its tab in tmux, kitty, WezTerm, Ghostty or Konsole,
and raises its window on Sway, Hyprland, niri, KDE Plasma and X11, and on GNOME
with the Claude Agents shell extension turned on. Otherwise it opens the agent
view. Only one tray runs per session; a second launch exits.
.PP
It also sends a notification when a session needs you, when one finishes, and
when the 5-hour or weekly usage reaches 80%.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-jump
Go to the session that needs you, else to one whose turn it is, else open the
agent view. A running tray does the jump; with none running, this launch
becomes the tray. Meant for a keyboard shortcut.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-agents-status.json
A copy of the Claude Code status line input, read for the usage limits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claude-agents-status (1)
